{% macro num(n) %}<a href="prov/{{ n.prov_id }}.html"><span data-prov="{{ n.prov_id }}">{{ n.text }}</span></a>{% endmacro %}
{% macro dash() %}-{% endmacro %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>AI spend memo</title>
<style>
body { font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 62rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1rem; color: #1b1f24; background: #fff; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem; display: block; overflow-x: auto; }
th, td { border-bottom: 1px solid #d0d7de; padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
th:first-child, td:first-child { text-align: left; }
.banner { border-left: 4px solid #9a6700; background: #fff8c5; padding: 0.6rem 1rem; }
.warning { border-left: 4px solid #cf222e; background: #ffebe9; padding: 0.6rem 1rem; }
a { color: inherit; text-decoration: underline dotted; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  body { color: #e6edf3; background: #0d1117; }
  th, td { border-bottom-color: #30363d; }
  .banner { background: #3b2e00; border-left-color: #d4a72c; }
  .warning { background: #3d1418; border-left-color: #f85149; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>AI spend memo for <time datetime="{{ month }}">{{ month }}</time></h1>
<p class="banner" id="planted">The company in this memo is made up and its effects are planted: the generator chose how much AI helps each team, and kept the answer in a file the method never reads. Recovering planted effects shows that the method works. It is not a finding about any real company.</p>
<p>Company AI spend in <time datetime="{{ month }}">{{ month }}</time> was {{ num(headline) }}. Every number below links to the source rows that produced it.</p>

<h2 id="pays-off">Does our AI spend pay off?</h2>
<p>A return is reported only for a team that has a fair comparison: teams that did not yet have AI tools at the time. Everywhere else the answer is unmeasured, with the reason. An effect is in log points of the team's own output, close to a percentage change when small, with a <span class="lit">95%</span> interval. The return multiple is the dollar value of the extra output divided by the AI spend in the same window, and one is break-even.</p>
<table id="return">
<thead><tr><th>Team</th><th>Status</th><th>Effect</th><th>Interval</th><th>AI spend</th><th>Output value</th><th>Return multiple</th><th>Return interval</th><th>Verdict</th><th>Share of payroll</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for t in teams %}
<tr><td>{{ t.name }}</td><td>{{ t.status }}{% if t.reason %} (<code>{{ t.reason }}</code>){% endif %}</td>
{% if t.measured %}
<td>{{ num(t.effect) }}</td><td>[{{ num(t.lo) }}, {{ num(t.hi) }}]</td>
{% if t.roi %}
<td>{{ num(t.roi.spend) }}</td><td>{{ num(t.roi.benefit) }}</td><td>{% if t.roi.multiple %}{{ num(t.roi.multiple) }}{% else %}{{ dash() }}{% endif %}</td>
<td>{% if t.roi.lo and t.roi.hi %}[{{ num(t.roi.lo) }}, {{ num(t.roi.hi) }}]{% else %}{{ dash() }}{% endif %}</td><td>{{ t.roi.verdict }}</td>
{% else %}
<td>{{ dash() }}</td><td>{{ dash() }}</td><td>{{ dash() }}</td><td>{{ dash() }}</td><td>no value per unit entered</td>
{% endif %}
{% else %}
<td>{{ dash() }}</td><td>{{ dash() }}</td><td>{{ dash() }}</td><td>{{ dash() }}</td><td>{{ dash() }}</td><td>{{ dash() }}</td><td>{{ dash() }}</td>
{% endif %}
<td>{% if t.share %}{{ num(t.share) }}{% else %}{{ dash() }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
{% if company_share %}
<tr><td>Company</td><td colspan="8"></td><td>{{ num(company_share) }}</td></tr>
{% endif %}
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Teams without a figure</h3>
<ul>
{% for t in unmeasured %}
<li>{{ t.name }}: {% if t.status == 'control' %}control. It has had no AI tools in the whole history, so there is nothing to compare, and it is the comparison for the others.{% else %}unmeasured, <code>{{ t.reason }}</code>: {{ t.why }} No return is reported for it.{% endif %}</li>
{% else %}
<li>None.</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% if sensitivity.rows %}
<h3>How the return changes with the value per unit</h3>
<p>The value per unit is an assumption. The table scales it by each multiplier and shows the return multiple, then the share of draws of the value in which the team still pays off.</p>
<table id="sensitivity">
<thead><tr><th>Team</th>{% for m in sensitivity.multipliers %}<th>{{ num(m) }}&times;</th>{% endfor %}<th>Pays off in this share of draws</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for r in sensitivity.rows %}
<tr><td>{{ r.name }}</td>{% for cell in r.cells %}<td>{% if cell %}{{ num(cell) }}{% else %}{{ dash() }}{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}<td>{% if r.survives %}{{ num(r.survives) }}{% else %}{{ dash() }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="next-dollar">Where does the next dollar go?</h2>
<p>The next dollar goes where the measured marginal return is highest. Unmeasured teams get an experiment before they get budget.</p>
{% if allocation.rows %}
{% if allocation.degenerate %}
<p class="warning" id="degenerate">Allocation degenerate: fewer than two teams are funded, or every funded team is at its cap, so this split says little about where the money should go.</p>
{% endif %}
<p>Monthly increment to allocate: {{ num(allocation.budget) }}.</p>
<table id="allocation">
<thead><tr><th>Team</th><th>Increment</th><th>Funded in this share of draws</th><th>At cap</th><th>Curve</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for r in allocation.rows %}
<tr><td>{{ r.name }}</td><td>{{ num(r.amount) }}</td><td>{{ num(r.funded) }}</td><td>{{ 'yes' if r.capped else 'no' }}</td><td>{% if r.identified is none %}{{ dash() }}{% elif r.identified %}identified{% else %}not identified{% endif %}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{% else %}
<p>No allocation was written for this month: it needs a monthly increment and a measured team with a return.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="test-next">What should we test next?</h2>
{% if agenda.rows %}
<table id="agenda">
<thead><tr><th>Team</th><th>Why unmeasured</th><th>Design</th><th>Per arm</th><th>Months</th><th>Smallest effect it can detect</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for r in agenda.rows %}
<tr><td>{{ r.name }}</td><td><code>{{ r.reason }}</code></td><td>{{ r.design }}</td><td>{% if r.n %}{{ num(r.n) }}{% else %}{{ dash() }}{% endif %}</td><td>{% if r.length %}{{ num(r.length) }}{% else %}{{ dash() }}{% endif %}</td><td>{% if r.delta %}{{ num(r.delta) }}{% else %}{{ dash() }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{% endif %}
{% if agenda.missing %}
<p>No experiment has been designed yet for: {{ agenda.missing | join(', ') }}.</p>
{% elif not agenda.rows %}
<p>Every team is either measured or the control, so there is nothing to test.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if assumptions %}
<h2 id="assumptions">What the figures assume</h2>
<p>The value of one unit of each measured team's output, in dollars, from the configuration. These are assumptions, not findings.</p>
<table id="values">
<thead><tr><th>Team</th><th>Unit</th><th>Low</th><th>Base</th><th>High</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for a in assumptions %}
<tr><td>{{ a.name }}</td><td>{{ a.unit }}{% if a.kind == 'team_level' %}, per month of change{% endif %}</td><td>{{ num(a.low) }}</td><td>{{ num(a.base) }}</td><td>{{ num(a.high) }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{% endif %}
{% macro source(r) -%}
<cite class="lit">{% if r.url %}<a href="{{ r.url }}">{{ r.source }}</a>{% else %}{{ r.source }}{% endif %}</cite>{% if r.quote %}: <q class="lit">{{ r.quote }}</q>{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
{% if calibration %}
<h2 id="calibration">How the planted effects were calibrated</h2>
<p>The planted effects were calibrated to published studies. A study counts as measuring the same kind of work only when it measured the team's own task; otherwise the team's effect is carried over from the nearest work that was measured.</p>
{% set different = calibration | selectattr('extrapolated') | list %}
{% set same = calibration | rejectattr('extrapolated') | list %}
{% if different %}
<p>These teams' planted effects come from studies that measured different work:</p>
<ul id="calibration-different">
{% for r in different %}
<li>{{ r.name }}: {{ source(r) }}. The study measured different work.</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}
{% if same %}
<p>These teams' planted effects come from studies that measured the same kind of work:</p>
<ul id="calibration-same">
{% for r in same %}
<li>{{ r.name }}: {{ source(r) }}.</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% include "benchmark.html.j2" %}
<p>Build facts for any number (code version, producer, checks) are not on these pages; <code>roi explain</code> prints them with the stored record.</p>
</body>
</html>
